{"id":"VHH__tool__noise2d_fractal","collection":"VHH","category":"tool","source_path":"VHH/tool/noise2d_fractal.json","root_names":["VHH::Tool::noise2d_fractal"],"counts":{"nodes":44,"connections":90,"values":34,"overloads":1},"documentation_summary":"Component Compound - this compound is a component in the the displacer ecosystem. Fractal Noise - One of the pre-made noise fields. The default fractal noise field.","documentation_search":"noise2d fractal Component Compound - this compound is a component in the the displacer ecosystem. Fractal Noise - One of the pre-made noise fields. The default fractal noise field. Input mask Scalar field mask on the outgoing field. warp vector field Domain warp on the outgoing field. field weight Overall weight of this field from 0-1. magnitude The magnitude of the noise. num frequencies This is the total number of noise frequencies to sum. Generally as this number increases there will be more detail or small scale noise. The value does not need to be an integer. frequency This is the base frequency of the fractal noise. Higher values have finer detail. frequency ratio This is the ratio of each noise frequency to the previous. ratio This is the ratio of magnitude of each noise frequency to the previous. If it is the same as frequency ratio then the magnitude of each noise will be the same relative to its scale. time A scalar field with the time to sample the noise at. time ratio This is the ratio of how fast the different noise frequencies animate. If the value is 1.0 then the frequencies all animate the same relative to their scale. adjust field An fCurve allowing you to adjust the field across values. translate Move the field. rotate Rotate the field. scale Scale the field. invert mask Inverts the scalar field mask. adjust mask A curve input that adjusts the scalar field mask. warp amount The amount to warp the field based on the field used as a domain warp. sharpen When this is selected, the field's opwn gradient is used for a domain warp. At lower values this has the effect of \"sharpening\" the field. Output fractal noise field The field result ready to be used.","port_names":["adjust_field","adjust_mask","field_weight","fractal_noise_field","frequency","frequency_ratio","invert_mask","magnitude","mask","num_frequencies","ratio","rotate","scale","seed","sharpen","time","time_ratio","translate","warp_amount","warp_vector_field"],"node_types_search":["Core::Conversion::degrees_to_radians","Core::Fields::advect_field","Core::Fields::fcurve_field","Core::Fields::field_is_empty","Core::Fields::fractal_noise_field","Core::Fields::gradient_field","Core::Fields::scalar_field","Core::Fields::transform_field","Core::Graph::pass","Core::Logic::equal","Core::Logic::if","Core::Math::SRT_to_matrix","Core::Math::add","Core::Math::clamp","Core::Math::divide","Core::Math::euler_to_quaternion","Core::Math::lerp","Core::Math::multiply","Core::Math::negate","Core::Math::subtract","Unknown","VHH::Core::Fields::change_range_field","adjust_the_field","change_range_field","maskWerks"],"dependencies_search":["VHH::Core::Fields::change_range_field"],"roots":[{"overload_index":0,"name":"VHH::Tool::noise2d_fractal","uri_imported":"stream:/bifrostGraphShape1","is_default_overload":null,"metadata":{"documentation":"../docs/noise2d_fractal.md","_sections":[{"type":"backdrop","title":"Warp"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Transform"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Field Weight"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Mask"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Adjust"}]},"documentation_file":"VHH/docs/noise2d_fractal.md","documentation":"### ***noise2d_fractal***\n<font size = 1>**Component Compound** - this compound is a component in the the *displacer* ecosystem.<br /><br /></font>\n<font size = 2>**Fractal Noise** - One of the pre-made noise fields.  The default fractal noise field.</font><br />\n\n\n***\n## Input\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***mask***</span>\n<br />Scalar field mask on the outgoing field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***warp_vector_field***</span>\n<br />Domain warp on the outgoing field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***field_weight***</span>\n<br />Overall weight of this field from 0-1.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***magnitude***</span>\n<br />The magnitude of the noise.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***num_frequencies***</span>\n<br />This is the total number of noise frequencies to sum. Generally as this number increases there will be more detail or small scale noise. The value does not need to be an integer.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***frequency***</span>\n<br />This is the base frequency of the fractal noise. Higher values have finer detail.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***frequency_ratio***</span>\n<br />This is the ratio of each noise frequency to the previous.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***ratio***</span>\n<br />This is the ratio of magnitude of each noise frequency to the previous. If it is the same as frequency_ratio then the magnitude of each noise will be the same relative to its scale.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***time***</span>\n<br />A scalar field with the time to sample the noise at. \n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***time_ratio***</span>\n<br />This is the ratio of how fast the different noise frequencies animate. If the value is 1.0 then the frequencies all animate the same relative to their scale.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***adjust_field***</span>\n<br />An fCurve allowing you to adjust the field across values.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***translate***</span>\n<br />Move the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***rotate***</span>\n<br />Rotate the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***scale***</span>\n<br />Scale the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#E69963\">***invert_mask***</span>\n<br />Inverts the scalar field mask.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***adjust_mask***</span>\n<br />A curve input that adjusts the scalar field mask.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***warp_amount***</span>\n<br />The amount to warp the field based on the field used as a domain warp.\n\n<span style=\"color:#E69963\">***sharpen***</span>\n<br />When this is selected, the field's opwn gradient is used for a domain warp.  At lower values this has the effect of \"sharpening\" the field.\n\n\n***\n## Output\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***fractal_noise_field***</span>\n<br />The field result ready to be used.","ports":[{"name":"magnitude","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"4f"},{"name":"num_frequencies","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"12f"},{"name":"frequency","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"0.0500000007f"},{"name":"ratio","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"0.5f"},{"name":"frequency_ratio","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"0.5f"},{"name":"time","direction":"input","type":"Core::Fields::ScalarField"},{"name":"time_ratio","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"1.5f"},{"name":"seed","direction":"input","type":"long","default":"0"},{"name":"translate","direction":"input","type":"Math::float3","default":{"x":"0f","y":"0f","z":"0f"}},{"name":"scale","direction":"input","type":"Math::float3","default":{"x":"1f","y":"1f","z":"1f"}},{"name":"rotate","direction":"input","type":"Math::float3","default":{"x":"0f","y":"0f","z":"0f"}},{"name":"mask","direction":"input","type":"Core::Fields::ScalarField"},{"name":"adjust_mask","direction":"input","type":"Math::FCurve","default":{"version":"1","preExtrapolation":"0","postExtrapolation":"0","points":[{"point":{"locked":"1","interpolation":"2","pcn":{"xp":"-0.40000000000000002","yp":"0","x":"0","y":"0","xn":"0.40000000000000002","yn":"0"}}},{"point":{"locked":"1","interpolation":"2","pcn":{"xp":"0.59999999999999998","yp":"1","x":"1","y":"1","xn":"1.3999999999999999","yn":"1"}}}]}},{"name":"warp_vector_field","direction":"input","type":"Core::Fields::VectorField"},{"name":"warp_amount","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"0.339300007f"},{"name":"sharpen","direction":"inpu